1
00:00:06,791 --> 00:00:10,875
In the end, I didn't
really do anything at all.

2
00:00:10,958 --> 00:00:12,249
I wonder if they'll be mad.

3
00:00:13,166 --> 00:00:16,374
(wall rumbling)

4
00:00:16,458 --> 00:00:18,249
(wall exploding)

5
00:00:21,459 --> 00:00:22,917
Ah.

6
00:00:23,001 --> 00:00:24,375
You on the other hand, though,

7
00:00:25,834 --> 00:00:27,792
you really worked way too hard.

8
00:00:30,084 --> 00:00:31,084
Awe.

9
00:00:32,418 --> 00:00:34,085
(gasps)

10
00:00:36,085 --> 00:00:39,710
(chuckles) Oh, you poor thing.

11
00:00:39,793 --> 00:00:41,209
(eerie music)

12
00:00:45,669 --> 00:00:48,045
Shall I put you
out of your misery?

13
00:00:50,669 --> 00:00:51,669
Hold on now.

14
00:00:53,377 --> 00:00:55,336
Don't go acting on
your own, human,

15
00:00:56,210 --> 00:00:57,754
or you'll die.

16
00:00:57,837 --> 00:01:00,920
Oh, stop, I was just being kind,

17
00:01:01,004 --> 00:01:03,128
which a curse might
not quite understand.

18
00:01:04,670 --> 00:01:08,004
(eerie music continues)

19
00:01:11,296 --> 00:01:13,212
So, got the goods?

20
00:01:13,296 --> 00:01:16,047
(chuckles) Without a hitch.

21
00:01:17,463 --> 00:01:21,755
All six of the special-grade
Sukuna's Finger cursed objects

22
00:01:21,838 --> 00:01:24,339
that Jujutsu High possessed,

23
00:01:24,422 --> 00:01:26,630
and the other
special-grade cursed object,

24
00:01:26,714 --> 00:01:29,339
Cursed Wombs Death
Paintings, One through Three.

25
00:01:32,422 --> 00:01:34,339
[Suguru] Most of the
temples at Jujutsu High

26
00:01:34,422 --> 00:01:35,505
are actually just a facade.

27
00:01:37,049 --> 00:01:40,673
Tengen's barrier keeps their
positions changing every day.

28
00:01:42,923 --> 00:01:46,381
And within those, only one
of over a thousand doors

29
00:01:46,465 --> 00:01:48,631
actually leads to the storeroom

30
00:01:48,715 --> 00:01:51,799
that holds cursed objects
as dangerous as the fingers.

31
00:01:56,507 --> 00:01:58,841
Each day, only Tengen knows

32
00:01:58,924 --> 00:02:01,257
which door leads to
the true storehouse,

33
00:02:01,341 --> 00:02:03,842
so I doubt anyone
will interfere.

34
00:02:03,925 --> 00:02:05,276
Who's this Tengen
you're talking about?

35
00:02:05,300 --> 00:02:08,300
A sorcerer with
immortality technique.

36
00:02:08,383 --> 00:02:11,884
Ah! He must be even
stronger than Gojo!

37
00:02:11,967 --> 00:02:14,675
Immortality, but
not eternal youth.

38
00:02:14,759 --> 00:02:17,509
You can think of him
as sort of just a tree.

39
00:02:17,593 --> 00:02:19,360
Tengen basically doesn't
interfere with the world,

40
00:02:19,384 --> 00:02:22,384
aside from maintaining barriers,

41
00:02:22,468 --> 00:02:24,301
so you really don't
have to worry about him.

42
00:02:24,384 --> 00:02:28,135
Remember the finger we
let Jujutsu High retrieve?

43
00:02:29,260 --> 00:02:31,469
I put a charm comprised of
Mahito's cursed energy on it

44
00:02:31,552 --> 00:02:33,302
before they collected it.

45
00:02:33,385 --> 00:02:35,844
It's under a single-layer seal,

46
00:02:35,927 --> 00:02:37,344
so they won't
bother to remove it.

47
00:02:37,427 --> 00:02:40,510
He'll be able to find it easily.

48
00:02:40,594 --> 00:02:42,136
And are there gatekeepers?

49
00:02:42,219 --> 00:02:43,678
Tengen does keep two attendants

50
00:02:43,762 --> 00:02:46,012
between the door
and the storeroom.

51
00:02:46,136 --> 00:02:47,553
Both chumps.

52
00:02:47,636 --> 00:02:50,887
More importantly, before
the veil actually goes down,

53
00:02:50,970 --> 00:02:51,845
I'd like you to very quietly

54
00:02:51,928 --> 00:02:55,346
thin out the sorcerers
stationed at the school

55
00:02:55,429 --> 00:02:57,137
to lighten the burden on Hanami.

56
00:02:57,220 --> 00:02:58,220
Mm-hmm.

57
00:02:58,471 --> 00:02:59,387
[Hanami] Why not
just seal Satoru Gojo

58
00:02:59,471 --> 00:03:01,387
inside the veil while
we have the chance?

59
00:03:03,137 --> 00:03:04,322
[Suguru] Because we don't
want to draw his attention

60
00:03:04,346 --> 00:03:06,889
toward Mahito's main mission.

61
00:03:10,430 --> 00:03:12,680
And we need him to
exercise his full power,

62
00:03:12,764 --> 00:03:15,180
or it won't be a
proper test of the veil.

63
00:03:15,263 --> 00:03:18,513
Trapping the students
inside will be more effective.

64
00:03:18,597 --> 00:03:21,431
[Hanami] Is it okay to
kill all but Sukuna's vessel?

65
00:03:21,514 --> 00:03:23,324
[Suguru] That's fine, but
I wouldn't recommend it.

66
00:03:23,348 --> 00:03:25,306
[Hanami] Hmm?

67
00:03:27,431 --> 00:03:29,222
[Suguru] So far,
Sukuna's actions

68
00:03:29,306 --> 00:03:31,015
have not been quite
what I expected.

69
00:03:32,389 --> 00:03:35,390
This is just my
guess, but I believe

70
00:03:35,474 --> 00:03:36,307
one of the other students acts

71
00:03:36,390 --> 00:03:39,307
as kind of a land
mine for Sukuna.

72
00:03:42,557 --> 00:03:45,725
Worst case scenario,
if we step on that,

73
00:03:45,808 --> 00:03:47,683
all of our current
plans will be ruined.

74
00:03:47,767 --> 00:03:48,933
Then why don't we just go

75
00:03:49,017 --> 00:03:50,933
and kidnap Itadori
ahead of time?

76
00:03:51,017 --> 00:03:52,767
We'll be using him as a pawn.

77
00:03:52,850 --> 00:03:56,975
But Itadori, or rather
Sukuna himself,

78
00:03:57,059 --> 00:04:00,142
is also a type of
land mine for us.

79
00:04:03,559 --> 00:04:06,559
That applies to both
us and Jujutsu High.

80
00:04:06,642 --> 00:04:11,518
We shouldn't agitate it until
the moment we want more chaos:

81
00:04:11,602 --> 00:04:14,435
October 31st in Shibuya.

82
00:04:16,352 --> 00:04:19,810
Everything we can
use to seal Satoru Gojo

83
00:04:19,894 --> 00:04:21,769
we should keep in
reserve until then.

84
00:04:24,519 --> 00:04:27,853
We'll have a few curse
users accompany us, too.

85
00:04:28,853 --> 00:04:30,478
But Juzo Kumiya,
he's disposable.

86
00:04:30,561 --> 00:04:32,811
He's not the kind of person

87
00:04:32,895 --> 00:04:35,269
who can follow a plan
all the way through.

88
00:04:35,353 --> 00:04:36,936
He'll just get in our way later.

89
00:04:37,604 --> 00:04:40,145
And we'll have a different
human as a monitor

90
00:04:40,228 --> 00:04:43,520
for our test run of the
veil, so get along with them.

91
00:04:43,604 --> 00:04:46,270
Yeah, you hear that,
Jogo? So get going.

92
00:04:46,354 --> 00:04:48,395
(grunts) I'm not going, anyway.

93
00:04:52,730 --> 00:04:55,813
Come on, Hanami, wake up.

94
00:04:56,146 --> 00:04:57,146
Let's go.

95
00:04:57,938 --> 00:04:58,855
[Hanami] Mahito?

96
00:04:58,938 --> 00:04:59,938
Hm?

97
00:05:01,105 --> 00:05:03,856
[Hanami] Trying to pump
the brakes on my hostility

98
00:05:03,939 --> 00:05:05,481
is incredibly stressful.

99
00:05:09,731 --> 00:05:12,689
You're sounding more like
a curse every day, Hanami.

100
00:05:13,939 --> 00:05:17,024
(opening theme music)

101
00:05:19,190 --> 00:05:23,690
(singing in Japanese)

102
00:06:43,196 --> 00:06:44,488
(birds chirping)

103
00:06:44,571 --> 00:06:46,489
Next up are the casualties.

104
00:06:46,572 --> 00:06:49,114
Three second-grade sorcerers,

105
00:06:49,197 --> 00:06:51,114
one semi-first-grade sorcerer,

106
00:06:51,197 --> 00:06:53,530
five supervisors,
and two guards.

107
00:06:53,614 --> 00:06:56,447
They were all on
standby at the school

108
00:06:56,530 --> 00:06:58,364
and all of them were
there working separately

109
00:06:58,447 --> 00:07:00,032
from Gojo and Principal Yaga.

110
00:07:01,239 --> 00:07:03,115
We're still waiting on
the report from Ieiri,

111
00:07:03,198 --> 00:07:04,674
but we're nearly
certain it was the work

112
00:07:04,698 --> 00:07:07,990
of the same cursed spirit that
Nanami encountered before.

113
00:07:08,074 --> 00:07:09,448
(Satoru grunts)

114
00:07:09,531 --> 00:07:10,615
What do you think?

115
00:07:10,698 --> 00:07:12,659
Should we share this
information with the students

116
00:07:12,699 --> 00:07:14,033
and the other sorcerers?

117
00:07:15,532 --> 00:07:16,532
No.

118
00:07:16,616 --> 00:07:18,991
It's probably better to
keep this among ourselves.

119
00:07:19,075 --> 00:07:21,407
We don't want to give
curse users certainty

120
00:07:21,491 --> 00:07:23,616
that special-grade
objects were stolen.

121
00:07:23,699 --> 00:07:26,200
Has our captured
curse user spilled?

122
00:07:26,283 --> 00:07:28,658
(sighs) Well, it's no
problem getting him to talk.

123
00:07:28,742 --> 00:07:33,784
But what he says? It's all
just irrelevant nonsense.

124
00:07:33,867 --> 00:07:36,742
Although, it's interesting
that he's claiming

125
00:07:36,825 --> 00:07:38,409
he was only in the attack

126
00:07:38,493 --> 00:07:41,284
because he was ordered to
come as part of a certain deal.

127
00:07:42,743 --> 00:07:44,826
I just wanted to make
myself a coat rack.

128
00:07:44,910 --> 00:07:48,035
The monk promised me that.

129
00:07:48,118 --> 00:07:49,201
I don't know his name.

130
00:07:49,284 --> 00:07:51,577
In fact, I don't even know
if it was a man or a woman.

131
00:07:51,660 --> 00:07:55,577
Just a brat with
white hair in a bob cut.

132
00:07:55,660 --> 00:07:59,036
A mysterious androgynous
monk kid with a bob haircut.

133
00:08:00,119 --> 00:08:01,410
Ring any bells?

134
00:08:01,494 --> 00:08:03,995
Nah. The guy sounds
like a bullshitter.

135
00:08:04,079 --> 00:08:06,995
Have we got anyone
skilled at confessions?

136
00:08:07,079 --> 00:08:08,637
How did these outsiders
and a cursed spirit

137
00:08:08,661 --> 00:08:12,037
get through all of
Tengen's barriers?

138
00:08:12,120 --> 00:08:12,870
[Satoru] That was
probably the work

139
00:08:12,953 --> 00:08:15,037
of the special-grade
cursed spirit

140
00:08:15,120 --> 00:08:16,453
the students were fighting.

141
00:08:17,579 --> 00:08:19,579
That one has a unique presence.

142
00:08:19,662 --> 00:08:21,454
Even though it's
a cursed spirit,

143
00:08:21,537 --> 00:08:24,245
it's incredibly close
to a natural spirit.

144
00:08:24,329 --> 00:08:26,871
According to Aoi, it was
able to hide among plants,

145
00:08:26,954 --> 00:08:31,246
and Tengen's barrier doesn't
function against plants.

146
00:08:31,330 --> 00:08:33,705
Remember, Tengen's
barrier puts all its power

147
00:08:33,789 --> 00:08:36,039
into hiding, not protecting,

148
00:08:36,122 --> 00:08:38,705
so once you get
in, it's kind of weak.

149
00:08:43,873 --> 00:08:45,706
Are they worried
about Sukuna's fingers

150
00:08:45,790 --> 00:08:48,247
enhancing Yuji's potential?

151
00:08:48,331 --> 00:08:49,931
Or are they trying to
enhance themselves?

152
00:08:52,623 --> 00:08:55,331
Something isn't sitting right.

153
00:08:55,414 --> 00:08:56,624
Well, for the time being,

154
00:08:56,707 --> 00:08:58,707
at least our
students are all safe.

155
00:08:58,791 --> 00:08:59,874
(Gakuganji grunts)

156
00:08:59,957 --> 00:09:04,124
But obviously the exchange
event will have to be canceled.

157
00:09:04,207 --> 00:09:06,916
Hold on! Since when is that
a decision we get to make?

158
00:09:06,999 --> 00:09:08,666
[Group] Huh?

159
00:09:10,917 --> 00:09:12,750
So how's it possible
that you get along

160
00:09:12,833 --> 00:09:14,750
with a gorilla like Todo?

161
00:09:14,833 --> 00:09:16,958
Well, the two of us got along,

162
00:09:17,042 --> 00:09:20,291
but it was like, I mean, I
do remember everything,

163
00:09:20,375 --> 00:09:23,334
but it feels like I wasn't
exactly myself at the time.

164
00:09:23,417 --> 00:09:24,727
What do you mean?
Were you drinking?

165
00:09:24,751 --> 00:09:28,126
You seriously believe I
could've been drinking liquor

166
00:09:28,209 --> 00:09:28,918
in a situation like that?

167
00:09:29,001 --> 00:09:30,959
That woulda been insane.

168
00:09:32,376 --> 00:09:34,585
Anyway, I'm just
glad your injuries

169
00:09:34,668 --> 00:09:36,585
weren't too serious, Fushiguro.

170
00:09:36,668 --> 00:09:37,960
To your health and this pizza.

171
00:09:40,377 --> 00:09:40,919
[Fushiguro] You could've
brought me something

172
00:09:41,002 --> 00:09:42,960
easier to digest.

173
00:09:43,835 --> 00:09:44,835
No complaining.

174
00:09:47,419 --> 00:09:49,128
Apparently, I got off easier

175
00:09:49,211 --> 00:09:51,336
because my cursed
energy was all gone,

176
00:09:51,419 --> 00:09:53,544
and Ieiri was still
able to fix me up

177
00:09:53,628 --> 00:09:54,771
as soon as the
roots were removed.

178
00:09:54,795 --> 00:09:57,711
[Itadori] Huh, so
that's what happened?

179
00:09:57,795 --> 00:09:58,875
[Kugisaki] You should know.

180
00:09:58,920 --> 00:10:00,481
You fought against
them too, didn't you?

181
00:10:01,712 --> 00:10:02,629
Itadori.

182
00:10:02,712 --> 00:10:03,879
Huh?

183
00:10:03,962 --> 00:10:06,170
[Fushiguro] You know,
you've grown a lot stronger.

184
00:10:06,253 --> 00:10:07,629
Hm?

185
00:10:07,712 --> 00:10:09,170
Before,

186
00:10:09,253 --> 00:10:11,053
we both said that we
stood by our convictions.

187
00:10:12,587 --> 00:10:13,628
I still think that's true.

188
00:10:16,880 --> 00:10:17,963
But then on the other hand,

189
00:10:18,047 --> 00:10:21,797
one could say that we're
both wrong about all of that.

190
00:10:21,880 --> 00:10:23,880
Huh?

191
00:10:23,963 --> 00:10:25,838
Some questions don't
have any answers.

192
00:10:25,922 --> 00:10:27,881
Don't think so
hard. You'll go bald.

193
00:10:27,964 --> 00:10:31,339
You're right,
there is no answer.

194
00:10:31,422 --> 00:10:33,923
I know it's just a matter
of trying to accept it.

195
00:10:35,006 --> 00:10:37,255
But why accept
something you don't want?

196
00:10:38,297 --> 00:10:40,049
Only weak sorcerers do that.

197
00:10:42,757 --> 00:10:43,757
So I've decided

198
00:10:45,298 --> 00:10:46,465
I'll surpass you.

199
00:10:49,298 --> 00:10:51,007
(laughs) You never change.

200
00:10:51,091 --> 00:10:54,674
Did I get left out of
the conversation again?

201
00:10:54,758 --> 00:10:58,050
There ya go. That's my
brother and his friends for ya.

202
00:10:58,133 --> 00:10:59,383
Mm-hmm. Mm-hmm.

203
00:11:00,633 --> 00:11:01,817
Wait, where are
you going, Brother?

204
00:11:01,841 --> 00:11:04,174
Hey, hold up!

205
00:11:04,257 --> 00:11:07,009
Look, I'm grateful to you,
but come on, give me a break!

206
00:11:07,093 --> 00:11:08,093
You know damn well

207
00:11:08,134 --> 00:11:09,967
that I wasn't thinking
straight back then!

208
00:11:10,051 --> 00:11:11,467
[Todo] What are you saying?

209
00:11:11,550 --> 00:11:13,842
We've been so close ever
since middle school, Brother!

210
00:11:13,926 --> 00:11:15,217
[Itadori] Since middle school?

211
00:11:15,300 --> 00:11:17,258
I didn't go to your
middle school!

212
00:11:22,551 --> 00:11:24,676
[Miwa] Hello! Useless Miwa here.

213
00:11:25,010 --> 00:11:28,426
And even though I
call myself useless,

214
00:11:28,510 --> 00:11:30,886
I don't actually think
that I'm all that bad.

215
00:11:32,719 --> 00:11:34,594
But it is true that
while everyone else

216
00:11:34,677 --> 00:11:35,594
was risking their lives fighting

217
00:11:35,677 --> 00:11:37,803
during the special-grade
cursed spirit's attack,

218
00:11:37,886 --> 00:11:40,469
I was fast asleep.

219
00:11:40,552 --> 00:11:41,844
And now I feel ashamed.

220
00:11:44,678 --> 00:11:48,512
Also, I wonder who
broke my sword?

221
00:11:48,595 --> 00:11:50,054
Was it Mai's older sister?

222
00:11:51,595 --> 00:11:52,512
After all of that,

223
00:11:52,595 --> 00:11:54,030
we thought the exchange
event would be canceled,

224
00:11:54,054 --> 00:11:59,262
but now, after taking a
day off, here we all are.

225
00:12:00,930 --> 00:12:02,638
[Satoru] Play ball!

226
00:12:02,721 --> 00:12:04,763
[Miwa] Playing baseball!

227
00:12:04,846 --> 00:12:07,554
(upbeat theme music)

228
00:12:10,847 --> 00:12:12,889
(casual theme music)

229
00:12:15,389 --> 00:12:17,472
(birds chirping)

230
00:12:17,555 --> 00:12:21,680
So anyway, that happened
and some people died.

231
00:12:21,764 --> 00:12:23,264
But what now?

232
00:12:23,348 --> 00:12:24,140
Keep going?

233
00:12:24,223 --> 00:12:28,640
Uh, I have no idea
what to say to that.

234
00:12:28,723 --> 00:12:29,640
Get real.

235
00:12:29,723 --> 00:12:31,057
Huh?

236
00:12:31,140 --> 00:12:33,140
[Todo] The Exchange Event
will continue, of course!

237
00:12:34,057 --> 00:12:35,599
[Itadori] Todo!

238
00:12:36,808 --> 00:12:37,891
What are your reasons?

239
00:12:37,974 --> 00:12:40,724
For one, only those who
have a direct connection

240
00:12:40,808 --> 00:12:42,200
to the victims have any
right to mourn them.

241
00:12:42,224 --> 00:12:45,391
It would be rude of
us to butt in there.

242
00:12:46,391 --> 00:12:47,100
And secondly, if
people have died,

243
00:12:47,182 --> 00:12:49,517
that's all the
more reason for us

244
00:12:49,600 --> 00:12:51,809
to work to become stronger.

245
00:12:51,892 --> 00:12:53,558
Acquired strength can only come

246
00:12:53,642 --> 00:12:54,934
from the
accumulation of results.

247
00:12:55,017 --> 00:12:58,308
Tasting defeat and
savoring victory,

248
00:12:58,392 --> 00:12:59,951
these are the things
that lead us to grow!

249
00:12:59,975 --> 00:13:02,060
The most important thing now

250
00:13:02,143 --> 00:13:04,726
is for those results
to continue to exist.

251
00:13:04,810 --> 00:13:07,018
This is surprising. Todo
sounds almost reasonable.

252
00:13:07,102 --> 00:13:09,976
Reasonably crazy.

253
00:13:10,060 --> 00:13:11,160
Third, when a student feels like

254
00:13:11,184 --> 00:13:13,018
they weren't able to
bring out their best,

255
00:13:13,102 --> 00:13:16,144
it'll hang over
them until they die.

256
00:13:16,227 --> 00:13:16,936
[Satoru] How old are you?

257
00:13:17,019 --> 00:13:19,560
Yeah, I'm fine with all that.

258
00:13:19,644 --> 00:13:21,019
We'll still win anyway.

259
00:13:21,103 --> 00:13:22,769
He does have a point there.

260
00:13:22,852 --> 00:13:24,602
Kamo, shouldn't you be resting?

261
00:13:24,685 --> 00:13:25,103
I'm in.

262
00:13:25,185 --> 00:13:26,103
[Inumaki] Salmon.

263
00:13:26,185 --> 00:13:28,186
How do we pair up
for the individual fights?

264
00:13:28,269 --> 00:13:32,770
Huh? There are no
individual battles.

265
00:13:34,020 --> 00:13:36,228
The Exchange Event always has

266
00:13:36,311 --> 00:13:38,020
the principals of
the two schools.

267
00:13:38,104 --> 00:13:41,354
Each propose a form of
competition for the two days,

268
00:13:41,437 --> 00:13:43,354
or that's how it's
supposed to be.

269
00:13:43,437 --> 00:13:46,021
Every year 'til now, the first
day has been team battles

270
00:13:46,105 --> 00:13:48,562
and the second
individual battles.

271
00:13:48,646 --> 00:13:49,646
[Inumaki] Salmon.

272
00:13:50,021 --> 00:13:52,187
(all grumbling)

273
00:13:52,270 --> 00:13:54,151
I don't like routines
but this is how it's done.

274
00:13:54,188 --> 00:13:57,271
Every year we put the
competition methods here

275
00:13:57,355 --> 00:13:58,438
and pull one out.

276
00:13:58,522 --> 00:13:59,522
Huh?

277
00:14:03,855 --> 00:14:06,898
Principal Gakuganji's
previous visit was to discuss

278
00:14:06,981 --> 00:14:09,481
what items might be needed
on the day of the event.

279
00:14:11,065 --> 00:14:13,189
[Itadori] Huh? What?

280
00:14:14,314 --> 00:14:15,398
-Huh?
-Whoa!

281
00:14:15,481 --> 00:14:16,398
Baseball?

282
00:14:16,481 --> 00:14:17,648
You too?

283
00:14:17,731 --> 00:14:19,125
[Gakuganji] What's
going on here, Yaga?

284
00:14:19,149 --> 00:14:20,440
[Yaga] I don't know!

285
00:14:20,524 --> 00:14:22,042
I was sure I put
individual battles in there.

286
00:14:22,066 --> 00:14:25,440
Hey! Get back here, Satoru!

287
00:14:25,524 --> 00:14:27,982
(lively music)

288
00:14:32,733 --> 00:14:33,650
(Maki grunts)

289
00:14:33,733 --> 00:14:35,483
(Miwa grunts)

290
00:14:35,566 --> 00:14:36,650
Fly ball!

291
00:14:36,733 --> 00:14:41,441
Nishimiya, no! Don't run yet!

292
00:14:41,525 --> 00:14:42,691
[Satoru] Out!

293
00:14:42,775 --> 00:14:43,691
Huh? But why?

294
00:14:43,775 --> 00:14:46,317
Momo, if you don't know
the rules, then say so!

295
00:14:46,901 --> 00:14:49,275
I do know them! When
the ball's hit, I run!

296
00:14:50,901 --> 00:14:53,275
A sacrifice fly? What's that,
some new form of torture?

297
00:14:53,359 --> 00:14:55,901
[Iori] You're just plain stupid!

298
00:14:59,111 --> 00:15:01,276
[Kamo] I heard you
fought off a special-grade.

299
00:15:01,360 --> 00:15:03,276
Huh? Oh, yeah.

300
00:15:03,360 --> 00:15:06,693
Mostly thanks to
Todo and Gojo really.

301
00:15:06,777 --> 00:15:07,860
No helmet, dude?

302
00:15:08,235 --> 00:15:10,653
Itadori,

303
00:15:10,736 --> 00:15:13,319
why did you want to
be a jujutsu sorcerer?

304
00:15:13,403 --> 00:15:15,112
At first, it just
kinda happened,

305
00:15:16,403 --> 00:15:21,236
but I'm kind of a loner so I
want to save lots of people

306
00:15:21,319 --> 00:15:24,445
so that I'll have lots of them
watching over me when I die.

307
00:15:25,946 --> 00:15:27,529
[Young Kamo] If
you're not there, Mom,

308
00:15:27,612 --> 00:15:30,154
then I won't become
a jujutsu sorcerer!

309
00:15:30,237 --> 00:15:33,071
Listen, Noritoshi,
you have talent.

310
00:15:33,154 --> 00:15:36,154
You can use it to
save lots of people.

311
00:15:37,613 --> 00:15:39,493
-(Young Kamo sobbing)
-The more people you save,

312
00:15:39,571 --> 00:15:41,696
the more you'll be recognized.

313
00:15:41,780 --> 00:15:45,114
Then in turn, all kinds
of people will help you.

314
00:15:45,196 --> 00:15:48,279
You'll only be alone for now,

315
00:15:48,363 --> 00:15:51,572
and one day, once you've
become a great sorcerer,

316
00:15:52,781 --> 00:15:54,364
I know you'll come and get me.

317
00:15:58,239 --> 00:15:59,239
Okay.

318
00:16:00,115 --> 00:16:02,740
That's a good reason.

319
00:16:02,824 --> 00:16:03,907
Strike!

320
00:16:03,990 --> 00:16:05,407
Batter out! Change up!

321
00:16:05,490 --> 00:16:08,198
[Iori] Kamo, you'll never
get a hit if you don't swing!

322
00:16:10,865 --> 00:16:14,281
They call me Tanaka of Tohoku!

323
00:16:14,365 --> 00:16:16,533
No, Tanaka's the
Tanaka of Tohoku.

324
00:16:16,616 --> 00:16:17,199
And Tanaka's a pitcher!

325
00:16:17,282 --> 00:16:19,117
[Inumaki] Bonito flakes.

326
00:16:19,199 --> 00:16:20,199
(Kugisaki growls)

327
00:16:22,199 --> 00:16:23,199
Huh?

328
00:16:26,282 --> 00:16:28,200
What the hell is that?

329
00:16:28,283 --> 00:16:31,034
Uh oh, Kugisaki
snapped! It's a free-for-all!

330
00:16:32,283 --> 00:16:34,409
Hey, using a pitching
machine is against the rules!

331
00:16:34,492 --> 00:16:36,010
I don't know what
you're talking about.

332
00:16:36,034 --> 00:16:38,742
This is just a spare.
It's a spare Mechamaru.

333
00:16:38,826 --> 00:16:41,827
We had no other choice, since
your Panda broke our main one.

334
00:16:41,910 --> 00:16:44,160
Huh, a pitching machine, eh?

335
00:16:44,243 --> 00:16:46,077
I guess I don't understand,

336
00:16:46,160 --> 00:16:47,827
but you know a
lot about machines.

337
00:16:47,910 --> 00:16:48,910
Hey, are you an otaku?

338
00:16:49,576 --> 00:16:52,284
It's just one thing after
another with you, huh?

339
00:16:52,368 --> 00:16:55,577
And yet somehow
you're still a student here.

340
00:16:57,036 --> 00:16:59,577
(grunts) Fine! I'll
get a hit anyway!

341
00:17:00,869 --> 00:17:02,411
[Itadori] All right,
she got on base!

342
00:17:02,494 --> 00:17:04,452
[Fushiguro] Fueled by rage.

343
00:17:04,536 --> 00:17:07,662
(casual catchy music)

344
00:17:12,328 --> 00:17:13,328
[Satoru] Out!

345
00:17:23,746 --> 00:17:26,287
(intense music)

346
00:17:30,538 --> 00:17:32,914
(Mai scoffs)

347
00:17:48,540 --> 00:17:50,206
(Maki grunts)

348
00:17:52,581 --> 00:17:54,082
[Itadori] Yeah!

349
00:17:56,748 --> 00:17:58,707
Gone! Home run.

350
00:18:01,707 --> 00:18:02,624
Huh?

351
00:18:02,707 --> 00:18:03,624
Oh!

352
00:18:03,707 --> 00:18:05,041
Ah!

353
00:18:05,125 --> 00:18:06,416
Ah! Cheater!

354
00:18:07,166 --> 00:18:07,582
[Inumaki] Bonito flakes!

355
00:18:07,666 --> 00:18:09,874
Kugisaki, go back.

356
00:18:15,583 --> 00:18:17,875
Catcher, huh?

357
00:18:17,959 --> 00:18:19,279
As catcher, you'll
call the shots,

358
00:18:19,333 --> 00:18:22,500
lead the defense, et cetera.

359
00:18:22,583 --> 00:18:25,501
One has to say it's a fitting
position for my brother,

360
00:18:25,584 --> 00:18:28,168
but I want a real face-off,

361
00:18:28,251 --> 00:18:30,292
a face-off with Pitcher Itadori.

362
00:18:31,626 --> 00:18:32,626
Todo.

363
00:18:33,584 --> 00:18:35,334
You could have
been their pitcher.

364
00:18:35,418 --> 00:18:36,543
No, he couldn't.

365
00:18:36,626 --> 00:18:39,086
Mechamaru had to pitch
because it's all he can do.

366
00:18:40,752 --> 00:18:42,669
Promise me this, brother.

367
00:18:42,752 --> 00:18:45,502
In a second, if I hit a
home run right here,

368
00:18:45,585 --> 00:18:46,919
next time you'll pitch.

369
00:18:47,002 --> 00:18:48,002
Ow!

370
00:18:54,461 --> 00:18:57,711
(gasps) Todo! Hang in there!

371
00:18:57,795 --> 00:18:58,920
Hey, nice pitch!

372
00:18:59,003 --> 00:19:00,378
[Both] Nice pitch.

373
00:19:00,461 --> 00:19:02,586
-Nice pitch!
-Nice pitch, Maki!

374
00:19:02,670 --> 00:19:03,462
-Nice pitch!
-Really, it wasn't bad.

375
00:19:03,546 --> 00:19:05,963
-Way to go!
-That was a good one.

376
00:19:06,046 --> 00:19:07,379
-Cool, man.
-Nice pitch, Maki.

377
00:19:10,004 --> 00:19:10,921
Wow, bro.

378
00:19:11,004 --> 00:19:13,379
Everyone really hates
you. I mean, everyone.

379
00:19:19,839 --> 00:19:22,713
Do you still hate young Itadori?

380
00:19:22,797 --> 00:19:24,964
It's not about
liking or hating him.

381
00:19:25,047 --> 00:19:26,463
The fact is that Itadori

382
00:19:26,547 --> 00:19:29,339
isn't allowed to exist
under jujutsu laws.

383
00:19:29,423 --> 00:19:32,339
He's only still alive due
to Gojo's selfishness.

384
00:19:32,423 --> 00:19:34,589
We must not bend
the rules of the group

385
00:19:34,673 --> 00:19:37,256
for any one individual,

386
00:19:37,339 --> 00:19:39,965
especially as we know
that many others may die

387
00:19:40,048 --> 00:19:41,966
because Itadori lives.

388
00:19:42,549 --> 00:19:46,757
But there are lives that
were saved thanks to him, too.

389
00:19:46,841 --> 00:19:48,521
Case in point, he worked
together with Todo

390
00:19:48,549 --> 00:19:51,590
to fend off the special-grade.

391
00:19:51,674 --> 00:19:54,632
Not that this applies
only to our students,

392
00:19:54,715 --> 00:19:56,591
but they're going to
stack up many regrets

393
00:19:56,675 --> 00:19:58,050
as their lives go on.

394
00:19:59,508 --> 00:20:03,008
I wish I had done that.
I wish they'd done this.

395
00:20:03,092 --> 00:20:06,550
I should have said that. I
wish someone had told me this.

396
00:20:09,592 --> 00:20:11,592
To be honest with you,

397
00:20:11,676 --> 00:20:12,509
I don't know what
the right decision is

398
00:20:12,592 --> 00:20:15,009
when it comes to Itadori.

399
00:20:17,551 --> 00:20:21,802
For now, let's just
watch over him, all right?

400
00:20:21,885 --> 00:20:24,468
(energetic music)

401
00:20:25,468 --> 00:20:28,177
Whoa, he made it!

402
00:20:28,260 --> 00:20:31,010
Yeah, Inumaki's
surprisingly fast, huh?

403
00:20:31,094 --> 00:20:32,301
[Inumaki] Salted roe.

404
00:20:32,385 --> 00:20:34,803
[Iori] Mai, Miwa!
Watch out for the steal!

405
00:20:37,095 --> 00:20:39,511
How about we save our
regrets for another day?

406
00:20:40,719 --> 00:20:45,219
(energetic music continues)

407
00:20:59,513 --> 00:21:00,513
Nailed it.

408
00:21:06,430 --> 00:21:07,430
Yes!

409
00:21:17,431 --> 00:21:20,514
(Satoru laughing)

410
00:21:20,597 --> 00:21:24,848
[Gakuganji] Yaga, do
something about Gojo first.

411
00:21:25,974 --> 00:21:29,057
(closing theme music)

412
00:21:36,015 --> 00:21:40,474
(singing in Japanese)

413
00:22:55,604 --> 00:22:57,189
[Cast] Juju Stroll!

414
00:22:57,272 --> 00:22:58,272
[Inumaki] Salmon.

415
00:22:58,772 --> 00:23:02,230
I'll say rice.

416
00:23:02,313 --> 00:23:04,981
But then again, I
do like bread too.

417
00:23:05,064 --> 00:23:07,730
Hey, wait! Does it
come with roe on it?

418
00:23:07,814 --> 00:23:09,356
I'm rice.

419
00:23:09,440 --> 00:23:10,065
Rice, I suppose.

420
00:23:10,149 --> 00:23:12,648
What? No way, I'm a bread girl!

421
00:23:13,940 --> 00:23:15,190
[Inumaki] Salted rice ball.

422
00:23:15,273 --> 00:23:18,190
Obviously it's bread
because I'm a panda!

423
00:23:18,273 --> 00:23:20,273
You want me to kill you or what?

424
00:23:21,565 --> 00:23:22,858
I don't know.

425
00:23:22,941 --> 00:23:25,816
This one feels kind
of forced somehow.

426
00:23:25,899 --> 00:23:29,024
It's not you.
They're out of ideas.

427
00:23:29,108 --> 00:23:30,649
Time to go home.

428
00:23:30,732 --> 00:23:33,858
(intense music)

